desc:
TLDR: As stated this program is for when you don’t have much time to lift but still want to build muscle.  It’s more upper body focused on my weak points  so swap out exercises or +/- sets to change the muscle priority.  Or if you don’t want a really long Day 1 swap out stuff. Reorder or whatever like I said to your liking. I’d recommend keep the full body, anterior, posterior muscle split!

Nuance:

6x chest
6x side delt
8x Tricep
6x bicep
4x lats
5x upper back
4x abs
8x quads
6x hamstring

Day 1 is long because usually I find a big chunk of time in the middle of the week to be in he gym for a good hour to hour and twenty at most to enjoy lifting. By that point I’m just itching to lift so I have a lot of stuff Day 1. Day 2 and 3 I tried having be an upper lower but I found making it an anterior posterior split I could get better leg volume and upper body volume than making them separate days.

Also the progression scheme is a simple double progression. Don’t expect to add a rep every week unless you’re newer. I’d expect at least a rep every month if you’re more experienced. 

Get enough protein for yourself, and be at maintanence or a slight deficit (I’m currently in a -250 deficit) to ensure muscle gains. If you decide to bulk I’d personally increase the volume on Saturday/Sunday by a set or two. 

If I had less lifting experience I would consider reducing the volume for some of the muscle groups if it interferes with recovery and just focus on going hard 

Exercises: 

Cable Lateral raise; 
     You can do any lateral raise it doesn’t matter. Ive don’t dumbbells for 2 years and just wanted to switch it up

Chest press;
     I like this more than barbell because I feel my performance on barbell has a big variance like one week I’ll get 8 reps on my first set and next week I’ll get 4, but on the machine I’m consistent

Incline db bench; 
     I used to do smith machine incline but I did it for 2 years and I wanted a change. Make sure if you do a low incline you don’t arch much because that makes it mkre of a flat bench

Straight bar Pushdown;
     I like straight bar way mkre than rope. Keep form strict and full ROM

Overhead extension;
     Awesome movement always do

Bicep curl machine; 
     I don’t like other bicep movements other than the cable

Ab machine; 
     Always do some sort of abs

Single arm lat pull-down;
     I have some sort of problem with my back where I pull mkre with my right side so I do single arm

Cable row;
     My choice of upper back movement

Hammer curl db;
     Hammer curls are goated imo

Bench bb;
     Here just to maintain my strength and technique 


Leg press;
     Nice movement for my quads personally

Back extension;
     Never don’t do this, my overall back health and hamstring glute strength has improved dramatically 

Seated hamstring;
     Hamstrings always cooked

Stiff leg deadlift
     If I do RDL’s I always seem to use my back but when I do them stiff I don’t have that

Leg extension;
     GOATED
